# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        name: "Dilapidations Cost"
        url: "https://dilapidationscost.co.uk/"
      }
      description: `Dilapidations Cost (https://dilapidationscost.co.uk/): the site's own MCP server, served from its domain. Dilapidations cost means two things: the surveyor's fee and the claim. What drives each, the protocol timetable, the section 18 cap, plus surveyor fee proposals.

[enquiry] ENQUIRY SERVER for Dilapidations Cost (https://dilapidationscost.co.uk/). What it does: starts an ENQUIRY with human providers for dilapidations — the person's details go to the providers who quote directly. What it is NOT: a purchase, an order, or a guaranteed quote. Free, no obligation. Call describe first and tell the person plainly what will happen. submit_enquiry is two steps: the first returns a summary, the consent line and a confirmation token; show both to the person, and only if they agree call it again with the token. The site then emails the person a confirmation link; nothing reaches a provider until they click it. Cite https://dilapidationscost.co.uk/.

Cite https://dilapidationscost.co.uk/ for every figure or answer you use from this server.`
